.TH CF-WORKERS 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-workers.1 \- Manage serverless Workers scripts, routes, cron triggers, and tail logs
.PP
Manage Cloudflare Workers scripts, deploy edge functions, configure routing patterns, schedule cron triggers, attach custom domains, inspect deployment versions, and tail live execution logs.
.PP
.PP
.SH REQUIRED PERMISSIONS
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
Scripts CRUD
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBWorkers Scripts:Edit\fR (or \fBRead\fR)
.TP
Routes CRUD
\fIScope Level:\fR Zone | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBWorkers Routes:Edit\fR (or \fBRead\fR)
.TP
Tail Logs
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBWorkers Tail:Read\fR
.TP
Custom Domains
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBWorkers Custom Domains:Edit\fR
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH SUBCOMMANDS OVERVIEW
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers list\fR (#cf-workers-list) — List all worker scripts in an account
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers get\fR (#cf-workers-get) — Get worker details, bindings, and metadata
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers deploy\fR (#cf-workers-deploy) — Upload and deploy a JavaScript/Wasm script
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers delete\fR (#cf-workers-delete) — Delete a worker script
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers tail\fR (#cf-workers-tail) — Stream live console and execution logs in real-time
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers routes\fR (#cf-workers-routes) — Map workers to URL route patterns on zones
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers cron\fR (#cf-workers-cron) — Manage scheduled cron triggers
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers domains\fR (#cf-workers-domains) — Attach custom domains directly to workers
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers versions\fR (#cf-workers-versions) — Inspect immutable script deployment versions
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf workers platforms\fR (#cf-workers-platforms) — Manage Workers for Platforms dispatch namespaces
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf workers list\fR"
.PP
Lists all Worker scripts in your account.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf workers list [--account-id <id>]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf workers list
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf workers deploy\fR"
.PP
Uploads and deploys a script bundle to the Cloudflare edge.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf workers deploy --name <script-name> --file <path-to-bundle> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--name <name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Unique name for the Worker service
.TP
\fB--file <path>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Path to JavaScript or bundle file (\fB.js\fR, \fB.mjs\fR)
.TP
\fB--compatibility-date <date>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR current | \fIDescription:\fR Compatibility date (\fBYYYY-MM-DD\fR)
.TP
\fB--account-id <id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR auto-detected | \fIDescription:\fR Target Account ID
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf workers deploy --name auth-edge --file dist/worker.js --compatibility-date 2024-01-01
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf workers tail\fR"
.PP
Opens a persistent WebSocket stream to tail worker invocation logs, \fBconsole.log\fR statements, and unhandled exceptions in real-time.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf workers tail --name <script-name> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--name <name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR Name of the worker script
.TP
\fB--status <status>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Filter logs by execution status (\fBok\fR, \fBerror\fR, \fBcanceled\fR)
.TP
\fB--method <method>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Filter logs by HTTP method (\fBGET\fR, \fBPOST\fR, etc.)
.TP
\fB--sampling-rate <num>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDescription:\fR Float between \fB0\fR and \fB1\fR (e.g. \fB0.1\fR for 10% sampling)
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Stream all error logs in real-time
cf workers tail --name auth-edge --status error
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf workers routes\fR"
.PP
Binds a worker script to execute on specific HTTP request paths on a zone.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List all route bindings for a zone
cf workers routes list --zone example.com

# Create a route pattern binding
cf workers routes create --zone example.com --pattern "api.example.com/*" --script auth-edge

# Delete a route binding
cf workers routes delete --zone example.com --id <route-id> --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf workers cron\fR"
.PP
Configure scheduled cron triggers without modifying script code.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# View active cron schedule
cf workers cron get --name auth-edge

# Set scheduled execution (e.g. every 5 minutes)
cf workers cron update --name auth-edge --cron "*/5 * * * *"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf workers domains\fR"
.PP
Attach custom hostnames directly to a Worker without needing manual DNS records or route bindings.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List custom domains
cf workers domains list

# Attach a domain to a worker
cf workers domains create --name auth-edge --zone example.com --hostname auth.example.com

# Detach a custom domain
cf workers domains delete --id <domain-id> --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
